se are part of the test *source*, fine in repo. I'm comfortable.\n\nNow, gen_cloud in make — the current gen_cloud dir has stray artifacts (gen_cloud.exe, main.obj, pdb) lying in the source dir! Those are leftovers (gitignored, *.exe etc). In make we should build gen_cloud into build/tools. And those stray files in gen_cloud/ are untracked-but-gitignored; harmless but messy. Note: clean them or leave (gitignored). Mention in plan: they shouldn't be there; remove them.\n\nAlso common/ has stray .obj and .lib files (geometry_c.obj, lib_c.lib etc.) in source dir — gitignored, leftovers from old bat builds. Should be cleaned (they're in source tree). Mention cleanup.\n\nAlso `vc140.pdb` in root — stray. Gitignored (*.pdb). Cleanup.\n\nNow — what about the `format-check` including refs? The wildcard picks up t2_passport_cpp/ref.cpp etc. (gitignored refs exist locally). format-check will lint them. If we add t3/t4 refs as committed .cpp, they'll be formatted too. Good.\n\nWait, there's an issue: `format-check` currently includes ref.cpp/ref.c files that are gitignored. On a clean clone they won't exist (wildcard just skips missing). Fine.\n\nNow, also the CONFIG axis: currently CONFIG ?= debug; release flags exist. t1 was the only one with release support exercised. Plan should keep the CONFIG axis across all tasks (the Makefile already defines CONFIG_FLAGS per config; pattern rules use them). Good — nothing to do beyond verifying release builds for new tasks. § 4.7: debug+ASan is the only required build for этап 1; release is for later. So we just keep the axis.\n\nNow — think about test count and rule generation. Let me estimate t2: cpp: abc(65), float? t2 tests: norm(0), eof_name(66), empty_name(65), eof_vertexes(66), empty_vertexes(65), negative_vertexes(64), fractional(65), nan(65). That's 8 cpp + 8 c = 16 rules. t3: cpp: empty(66), not_digit(65), too_few(65), norm1(0), norm2(0), norm3(0) = 6, c=6 → 12 + mass(10/100/1e6) ×2 = maybe 6-8. t4: cpp: radius_empty(64), too