mmend the macro approach with a clear explanation, and structure the plan so we build it incrementally: first t2 with explicit rules (to confirm patterns & the checker tool), THEN introduce the macro when adding t3/t4 (when repetition becomes unbearable) — this matches \"повторила дважды — выноси\". Actually she already has the DRY principle. I'll propose: port t2 explicitly; when t3 arrives, the test rules for t3/t4 mostly share shape → factor into a macro then. Good staged approach.\n\nWait, actually the journal notes she's already aware of the \"повторила дважды — выноси\" self-review rule. Good.\n\nLet me also reconsider: is there a simpler pattern than .ok stamps for the bulk? Alternative: a single \"test\" that runs a script-like loop? No — § 4.9 п.2 forbids script orchestrators; each test = C/C++ exe or make target with honest deps. .ok stamps = good.\n\nNow, one more design point: the check tool + run_case both live in build/tools. run_case already builds. We add check_contains build rule. Also gen_cloud → build/tools. And refs → build/tools or per-task? refs are per-task (t3_bbox_ref.cpp) but build into build/tools? They're like test tools. Put ref build output in `$(BINDIR)\\tools\\t3_bbox_ref.exe` and `t4_filter_ref.exe`. Sources: where? `tests/t3_bbox_ref.cpp`, `tests/t4_filter_ref.cpp`? Or task dirs. Hmm. The .bat used ref.ps1 at root. Let me put ref sources in the task dirs (t3_bbox_cpp/ref.cpp, t4_filter_cpp/ref.cpp) — matches t1/t2 pattern (ref.cpp in task dir). But gitignore ignores t1/t2 refs (not t3/t4). For consistency of \"refs are committed\", maybe move all refs? Overkill. I'll place t3/t4 refs in task dirs as `ref.cpp` and REMOVE the gitignore entries for them (commit them). Actually to keep repo consistent, I'll propose: un-ignore refs (commit ref sources for all tasks as part of repo per § 4.9 п.3), OR at least commit t3/t4 refs. Hmm — § 4.9 п.3 explicitly says референс should be in repo. The student gitignored them earlier (2026-07-23 journal) — maybe to reduce noise. But for make mass tests we need them. I'll propose un-ignoring and committing the refs needed (t3/t4), and flag the t1/t2 ref situation as optional. Actually since t1/t2 refs are gitignored and unneeded, I'll leave them but note the inconsistency. Let me not overload the plan.\n\nLet me now also verify the t1 norm test uses findstr; we're replacing findstr with checker only for t2-t4 (per user choice). But maybe ALSO migrate t1's findstr to the checker for consistency? The user's choice was about t2-t4 Russian literals. t1's is ASCII findstr which works. But consistency argues for using checker everywhere. I'll propose migrating t1 norm test to the checker too (one unified mechanism), as a small optional step. Actually — better to keep t1 working as-is and switch t1 to checker at the end for uniformity. Let me include it as an optional \"унификация\" step.\n\nNow let me think about the actual sequence/steps for the plan, each a commit:\n\n**Этап A: инфраструктура**\n1. `tests/check_contains.cpp` — новый чекер (haystack file + needle file, байтовый поиск; пустой needle = проверка пустоты). Сборка в build/tools. Микро-тест чекера? Could test checker itself via a couple cases in make? Maybe later. At least compile+smoke.\n2. Makefile: правило сборки check_contains, добавить каталоги для t2/t3/t4, expect-каталог.\n3. gitignore: негация для tests/data и tests/expect (или naming), убрать gitignore-записи для t3/t4 refs.\n4. Удалить мусор из исходных каталогов (common/*.obj lib, gen_cloud/*, vc140.pdb) — они gitignored, чистота дерева.\n\n**Этап B: t2 (статик, без DLL)**\n5. Объекты/линковка: t2 main + string_utils (static) для c/cpp.\n6. Тесты t2: 8 случаев × 2 языка. Входы с русским именем — файл `tests/data/t2_norm_in.txt`; `type file | main`? Actually `< file` redirection is cleaner: `main.exe < in.txt`. run_case command: `\"$(T2_CPP_EXE) < $(DATA)\\t2_norm_in.txt > out.txt 2> nul\" 0 && check out.txt expect.txt`. \n   - Норм: выход содержит \"Фигура «звезда»: 6 вершин.\" (expect file CP1251).\n   - EOF/empty: use `type nul` / `< nul`. `< nul` gives empty stdin. Or `type nul`. Either.\n7. `make test` зелёный для t2; формат; коммит.\n\n**Этап C: t3 (DLL + массовые)**\n8. Объекты: string_utils/geometry _dll (c/cpp), DLL сборка common_cpp.dll/common_c.dll + import libs.\n9. Линковка t3 main против import lib; PATH в рецептах тестов.\n10. gen_cloud цель в make (build/tools/gen_cloud.exe).\n11. Референс t3: tests/t3_bbox_ref.cpp (C++), сборка, сравнение fc. Ожидания по ошибкам: checker + expect-файлы.\n12. Тесты t3: ошибки (empty 66, not_digit 65 с expect stderr, too_few 65 с expect), 3 норм-кейса (substring проверки через expect), массовые (10/100/10^6): gen_cloud --size --seed → cloud.txt (build), main < cloud > out, ref < cloud > refout, fc. \n13. Коммит.\n\n**Этап D: t4 (DLL, фильтр)**\n14. Линковка t4 против общих DLL (переиспользуем common_cpp.dll/common_c.dll — объекты уже есть; но t3/t4 оба используют DLL → общие).\n15. Референс t4: tests/t4_filter_ref.cpp.\n16. Тесты t4: radius error cases (64) с expect stderr; point error (65), empty (66); норм-кейсы; массовые.\n17. Коммит.\n\n**Этап E: унификация и закрытие**\n18. Перенос t1 norm на checker (опционально), удаление t1_build_and_test.bat... wait, удаление .bat всех задач (§ 4.9 п.1, одна точка входа). Проверка: чистый клон → make test зелёный одной командой.\n19. README: обновить раздел сборки/тестов (make покрывает t1–t4, убрать \"before make\" раздел про .bat?). Actually README \"before make\" section documents manual build — keep as historical? It documents the manual layer (valuable as learning). But § 4.9 says одна точка входа; README должен отражать make как основной путь. I'll propose updating README: make как основной путь, .bat удалены, структура обновлена.\n20. Финальная проверка § 4.7 (Debug+ASan), § 4.1 self-review, clang-format.\n\nAlso should verify: does make run under \"x64 Native Tools\" environment? cl/link must be on PATH. Yes,