RTS into common_cpp.dll/common_c.dll, main compiled WITHOUT /DCOMMON_STATIC (dllimport) and linked against import lib.\n\nSo the Makefile needs per-task/per-obj flags, not one generic rule. That's exactly the architecture point I flagged at the start of the plan (need separate `_dll` objects). I should connect this to the plan.\n\nLet me verify the string_utils/geometry .cpp — is there any place where struct Point has member functions? No, plain struct.\n\nAlso I should double check whether main.obj in the C version — same story. main.c uses struct Point, cos/sin. No parse_point. Good.\n\nNow, should I actually verify by attempting link? I'm in plan mode, read-only. I can run read-only commands like dumpbin (already did). I could check if link would fail by... no, that modifies output. Actually running `link /lib` or trying to link would create files — not allowed. I'll rely on analysis.\n\nActually, wait — I want to double check one more nuance: maybe main.obj DOES have __imp_ references that resolved fine because geometry_cpp.obj with COMMON_STATIC... no, main.obj had no parse_point reference at all. Confirmed.\n\nLet me also confirm the pattern rule truly doesn't add /DCOMMON_STATIC: yes, line 108: `$(CXX) /c /Fo:$@ $(CXXFLAGS) $<`. CXXFLAGS has no /DCOMMON_STATIC. And geometry_cpp.obj has explicit rule WITH /DCOMMON_STATIC (line 115-116). So the asymmetry the user noticed is real.\n\nSo the answer to \"почему это вообще работает?\":\n- t1 works by accident: no common function calls → COMMON_API irrelevant for main.obj.\n- The asymmetry is a latent bug that will surface the moment t2/t3/t4 enter make; the pattern rule must be refined (per-task defines), which ties into the already-planned static/DLL object split.\n\nLet me present this concisely and update the plan note.\n\nLet me also double-check whether there could be a subtlety: does t1 main.cpp perhaps use exit_codes.hpp only (namespace exit_code)? Yes, constants. Fine.\n\nOne more check: could the answer be